# Added 22 October 2026 (Phase 179): the 135 MB counted-knowledge cache is
# rebuilt by `corpus --refresh`; each re-written copy made a push too large
# for the git server, so it is kept out of version control.
# Widened 22 October 2026 (after Phase 179): the whole cache directory. The two
# word-address books beside it (about 1 MB each) are re-written on every
# corpus change too, so they were the same problem at a smaller size. All of
# it is rebuilt on first use (see STATUS.md, "Repository hygiene"), and
# tests/test_repository_hygiene.py fails if any of it is tracked again or if a
# tracked file grows past 10 MB.
